  <h1>08. Molecular-level correction (DFT+Σ) and length convergence</h1>
  <p class="page-meta"><strong>2026-06-26 · current frontier</strong> · A longer scattering region
    confirms the result; B3LYP orbital shifts computed as the input to the DFT+Σ level correction</p>

  <h2>Goal</h2>
  <p>Two things before the level-corrected transport: (1) confirm the conductance is converged once
     the <strong>scattering region</strong> (the central device between the two semi-infinite VSe₃
     electrodes) is made longer, and (2) compute the B3LYP→vdW-DF2 molecular-orbital energy shifts
     $\Delta_i$ that feed the DFT+Σ correction.</p>

  <div style="border:1px solid var(--border,#ccc);border-radius:6px;padding:0.6em 1em;margin:1em 0;background:rgba(127,127,127,0.06)">
    <strong>The story of this correction (v1 → why it was wrong → v2).</strong>
    <ol style="margin:0.4em 0">
      <li><strong>v1 (first attempt, Section C bottom).</strong> Built the level shift as
        $\Delta_i=\varepsilon(\text{B3LYP,VASP})-\varepsilon(\text{vdW-DF2,SIESTA})$, aligned by
        vacuum level. Reported device $T(E_F)$ 0.355→0.051 and a "frontier gap 0.18 eV". Full
        PDOS / $T(E)$ / eigenchannel / I–V figures were produced.</li>
      <li><strong>Why it was wrong.</strong> The two codes differ by a ~0.71 eV rigid offset that
        vacuum alignment does not remove (same-PBE test; even the explicit valence count differs,
        168 vs 74). This offset flips the virtual shifts negative, so the gap never opens. Worse,
        the vdW-DF2 frontier energy (≈$E_F$) then maps onto B3LYP's <em>virtual</em> LUMO+3/LUMO+4
        (spacing <strong>0.185 eV</strong>) — that is exactly the v1 "0.18", i.e. a mislabelled
        pair of virtual levels, not a HOMO–LUMO gap (the true gap is 0.75 eV).</li>
      <li><strong>v2 (fix, Section C top).</strong> Subtract only within each code by telescoping
        through PBE. Signs become physical (occ↓/virt↑), gap opens 0.75 eV, $T(E_F)$ 0.355→0.003.
        Quantitative caveats (image-charge, B3LYP-as-truth, non-SCF) are stated in
        <em>Physics validity</em>.</li>
    </ol>
    Section C below is ordered <strong>v2 (current) first, then the v1 disproof</strong>.
  </div>

  <h2>A. Scattering-region length convergence</h2>
  <p>The 60° heterojunction was relaxed and its transport recomputed with the scattering region
     extended from <strong>3 to 9 VSe₃ unit cells per electrode</strong> (cell-fixed relaxation,
     vdW-DF2; transport at electrode k-point grid 100, η = 0.005 eV). Geometry, molecular PDOS, and
     transmission all converge.</p>

  <h3>Relaxation — interface geometry converges by 7 unit cells</h3>
  <p>The interface bond lengths and the molecule–chain gap stop changing by 7 cells: the
     molecule–chain (Se···VSe₃) gap moves 50 → 8 → 1 mÅ and is stable at 9.</p>
