  <h3>What the v1 "0.18 eV gap" actually was</h3>
  <p>Aligning the two codes by vacuum level and reading the B3LYP levels at each vdW-DF2 orbital's
     energy exposes the error directly. vdW-DF2's HOMO/LUMO sit at −5.55 eV (near $E_F$). The
     B3LYP level that lands at that <em>same energy</em> is <strong>not</strong> the B3LYP HOMO
     (−6.59 eV, pushed far down by the code offset) but its <strong>virtual LUMO+3/LUMO+4</strong>:</p>
